# 7. DATABASE SECURITY — ROW LEVEL SECURITY

Enable and verify Row Level Security on every table containing private or merchant-controlled information.

Implement the following rules.

PUBLIC VISITORS:
- Can read active stores.
- Can read published products from active stores.
- Cannot read private merchant records.
- Cannot read private customer information.
- Cannot modify database records.

CUSTOMERS:
- Can view their own orders.
- Can create valid orders.
- Can manage their own addresses and favorites.
- Cannot view other customers' private information.
- Cannot change order prices.
- Cannot alter stock.
- Cannot change their own authorization role.

MERCHANTS:
- Can manage their own stores.
- Can manage their own products.
- Can view orders belonging to their stores.
- Can update authorized order statuses.
- Cannot access another merchant's private information.
- Cannot promote themselves to admin.

ADMIN:
- Can perform authorized moderation.
- Can suspend stores.
- Can moderate products.
- Can inspect platform orders.

Test RLS using actual authenticated users and database/API requests.

Do not rely on frontend route protection alone.

Do not expose the Supabase service-role key.

Do not expose database credentials.

