# 10. CHECKOUT AND ORDER PROCESSING — WITHOUT PAYMENTS

Implement a complete order-processing system without in-app payments.

The customer must not need to pay UgaByte to place an order.

## Checkout journey

1. Customer browses products.
2. Customer adds products to cart.
3. Customer opens checkout.
4. Customer enters full name.
5. Customer enters phone number.
6. Customer enters optional email.
7. Customer selects pickup or delivery.
8. Customer enters delivery information if needed.
9. Customer adds an optional note.
10. Customer reviews order details.
11. Customer submits order.
12. System validates the order server-side.
13. System checks product availability.
14. System recalculates prices.
15. System creates the order and item records atomically.
16. System updates stock safely.
17. System returns a unique order reference.
18. Customer sees an order confirmation.
19. Merchant receives the order in their dashboard.
20. Customer and merchant communicate directly about payment and fulfilment.

## Important checkout rules

- No in-app payment gateway.
- No payment credentials.
- No card collection.
- No wallet.
- No fake payment confirmation.
- No automated mobile money collection.
- No claim that UgaByte has received customer money.

Display:

"Your order has been submitted. The seller will contact you to confirm fulfilment and payment arrangements."

The order status and payment arrangements must not be confused.

## Order statuses

Implement:

- pending
- accepted
- processing
- ready
- dispatched
- completed
- cancelled
- rejected

Enforce valid status transitions.

## Inventory

Implement safe inventory handling.

- Do not permit negative stock.
- Recheck stock during order creation.
- Prevent overselling during simultaneous orders.
- Use database transactions or atomic database functions.
- Define and implement a consistent stock-restoration policy for cancelled or rejected orders.
- Preserve order item snapshots.

## Guest checkout

Support guest checkout where possible.

Guest customers must be able to submit orders using their name and phone number without creating an account.

Implement secure order references and appropriate protections against unauthorized order lookup.

Do not expose private customer data through predictable order IDs.

